{"meta":{"dataset":"state-courts","title":"State trial-court caseloads by court level, county and case type: Texas district, constitutional county and statutory county courts, fiscal years 2023–24 and 2024–25","version":"1.0.0","doi":"10.5281/zenodo.23723926","doiUrl":"https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23723926","conceptDoi":"10.5281/zenodo.23723925","license":"CC BY 4.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","attribution":"Source: Probative, State trial-court caseloads by court level, county and case type: Texas district, constitutional county and statutory county courts, fiscal years 2023–24 and 2024–25, version 1.0.0, https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23723926, licensed CC BY 4.0.","citation":"Probative. (2026). State trial-court caseloads by court level, county and case type: Texas district, constitutional county and statutory county courts, fiscal years 2023–24 and 2024–25 (Version 1.0.0) [Data set]. Zenodo. https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23723926","disclaimer":"Not legal advice. These are counts from the Texas Office of Court Administration's published statistics, kept for marketing planning. A case added is a new case or motion on a court's docket, not a person or a client. Check the Office of Court Administration's current report.","notice":"Probative is a marketing firm, not a law firm; not legal advice.","lastChecked":"2026-10-27","url":"https://probativegrowth.com/data/v1/state-courts/index.json","humanUrl":"https://probativegrowth.com/data/state-courts/","statusCodes":{"P":"primary source","S":"secondary source","D":"ABA model default","U":"open question"}},"summary":"How many cases are added to Texas trial-court dockets, by county, court level and case group, from the Office of Court Administration's annual statistical reports: district courts (civil, family, juvenile, criminal), constitutional county courts (civil, criminal, juvenile) and statutory county courts (civil, family, juvenile, felony, misdemeanor), for Texas fiscal years 2024